; Testing dirichlet_eq which observes that a Dirichlet draw equals a specific
; probability vector. The posterior on `p` should be a Pinned prior at that
; vector (mirrors `beta_observation.pluck` for `prob_eq`).
; The value uses matrix-literal syntax (curly braces, comma-separated) so it
; parses as a 1-D FloatMatrix rather than a Cons-list.
(query
  (let (p (dirichlet 1.0 1.0 1.0))
    (Posterior (dirichlet_eq p {0.2, 0.3, 0.5})
      (dirichlet_eq p {0.2, 0.3, 0.5}))))
